}
```

**POST request with a body:**
```javascript
const data = await fetchJSON("https://api.example.com/users", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
  body: JSON.stringify({ name: "Alice", age: 30 }),
});
```

### Key Details

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| `async/await` | Makes asynchronous code readable and linear |
| `response.ok` | Checks for HTTP status codes in the 200–299 range |
| `response.json()` | Parses the response body as JSON (also async) |
| `options = {}` | Allows passing any valid `fetch` options (method, headers, body, etc.) |

> **Note:** `fetch` only rejects on **network errors** (e.g., no connection). A `404` or `500` response is considered a *successful* fetch, which is why the `response.ok` check is important.

